B.Vj=new A.zS("flame",B.aa4,B.U3,B.UW,B.ux,B.Uj,B.TK,B.SF,B.ux,12)
B.NB=new A.bD("Every fire begins small. In the ashram at Yellapur, the morning havan is lit with a few dry twigs, a pinch of camphor and a single match. Nobody expects a blaze in the first minute.",null,null)
B.N7=new A.bD("The inner life begins the same way. A few quiet minutes before the house wakes, one chant said with attention, one sharp word held back. These are the twigs. They do not look like much, and that is exactly why we can begin today.",null,null)
B.Nq=new A.bD("Many seekers wait for the right time \u2014 after the exams, after the wedding, after retirement. But a fire does not need perfect weather. It needs a small, dry place and someone willing to strike the match.",null,null)
B.Na=new A.bD("Choose that place now. A corner of a room, a mat, a lamp. Return to it at the same hour tomorrow. Let the place itself begin to remember you.",null,null)
B.Nl=new A.bD("I praise Agni, the fire placed before all things. The very first word of the Rigveda is fire.","agnim \u012b\u1e37e purohitam","Rigveda 1.1.1")
B.a8O=s([B.NB,B.N7,B.Nq,B.Na,B.Nl],t.L4)
B.Mq=new A.ib("Kindling",9,B.a8O)
B.NE=new A.bD("A fire that is lit and then forgotten goes out. The flame asks for small offerings, given often: a stick now, a spoon of ghee a little later. Too much at once and it chokes; too little and it fades.",null,null)
B.ND=new A.bD("Practice is fed in the same measure. Twelve minutes every day will carry you further than two hours once a month. The body learns the rhythm long before the mind learns the meaning.",null,null)
B.MZ=new A.bD("Watch what you feed it. Good company, simple food, a little study and enough sleep are dry wood. Gossip, endless scrolling and late nights are wet wood \u2014 they give more smoke than light.",null,null)
B.N3=new A.bD("Some days the fire will burn low. You will sit down and feel nothing at all. Sit anyway, and offer the one stick you have. The embers are still warm, even when you cannot see them.",null,null)
B.Ns=new A.bD("Students often ask how they will know the fire is growing. You will notice it first in small things: you wait more patiently, you speak a little more slowly, you are less hurried to be right.",null,null)
B.a9J=s([B.NE,B.ND,B.MZ,B.N3,B.Ns],t.L4)
B.MB=new A.ib("Feeding the flame",58,B.a9J)
B.MG=new A.bD("Discipline has a hard reputation. We picture a strict teacher with a stick. But the Sanskrit word tapas simply means heat \u2014 the steady warmth that comes from steady effort.",null,null)
B.MP=new A.bD("A potter fires the clay so that it can hold water. Without the kiln, the most beautiful pot melts in the first rain. Tapas is that kiln. It turns good intentions into something that can carry weight.",null,null)
B.Nu=new A.bD("Lift yourself by your own self; do not let yourself sink.","uddhared \u0101tman\u0101tm\u0101na\u1e43 n\u0101tm\u0101nam avas\u0101dayet","Bhagavad Gita 6.5")
B.N_=new A.bD("Begin with one promise you can keep. Not ten. Wake at the same time for one month, or chant the Gayatri eleven times before your morning tea. Keep it on good days and on bad days, and slowly the promise begins to keep you.",null,null)
B.MJ=new A.bD("When you break it \u2014 and you will \u2014 do not scold yourself. Gently come back, the way you would add one more stick to the fire. Discipline is not never falling. It is always returning.",null,null)
B.Nd=new A.bD("In time the heat becomes light. What began as effort becomes ease, and what was a rule becomes a joy. That is the inner fire: not a flame that burns you, but one that lets you see.",null,null)
B.a6c=s([B.MG,B.MP,B.Nu,B.N_,B.MJ,B.Nd],t.L4)
B.Mv=new A.ib("The fire of discipline",114,B.a6c)
B.a74=s([B.Mq,B.MB,B.Mv],t.n4)
B.NF=new A.l_("inner-fire","The Inner Fire",172,3.4,"Practice","14 Jun 2026",B.Vj,"Guruji\u2019s short book on tapas \u2014 the quiet heat of daily practice. Using the image of the morning havan at the ashram, it shows how a small, steady effort slowly becomes a light you can live by. Practical and warm, easy to read one chapter at a time.",B.a74,!1)
B.a8U=s(["Sounds of the","Veda"],t.s)
B.UX=new A.i(1,0.07450980392156863,0.13725490196078433,0.24705882352941178,B.h)
B.RR=new A.i(1,0.17647058823529413,0.30980392156862746,0.5019607843137255,B.h)
B.v7=new A.i(1,0.9137254901960784,0.7372549019607844,0.3607843137254902,B.h)
B.U5=new A.i(1,0.9686274509803922,0.9058823529411765,0.7568627450980392,B.h)
B.Sn=new A.i(1,0.9529411764705882,0.9019607843137255,0.7843137254901961,B.h)
B.SA=new A.i(1,0.4980392156862745,0.6392156862745098,0.8392156862745098,B.h)
B.Vl=new A.zS("waves",B.a8U,B.UX,B.RR,B.v7,B.U5,B.Sn,B.v7,B.SA,16)
B.Nk=new A.bD("For thousands of years the Vedas were not read. They were heard. A teacher chanted, a student repeated, and the sound passed from mouth to ear across a hundred generations without a single page.",null,null)
B.MR=new A.bD("This is why the tradition cares so much about how a word is said. A mantra is not only its meaning. It is a shape of breath, a pattern of rising and falling, a vibration that settles the one who chants it.",null,null)
B.Nb=new A.bD("You do not need to understand every word to begin. A child learns a lullaby long before she knows what it means, and is comforted all the same. Let the sound work on you first; the meaning will follow.",null,null)
B.MC=new A.bD("Sit straight, so the breath has room. Chant a little slower than feels natural. Notice where the sound lives in your body \u2014 the chest, the throat, the space behind the eyes.",null,null)
B.a5Y=s([B.Nk,B.MR,B.Nb,B.MC],t.L4)
B.Mp=new A.ib("Why sound matters",11,B.a5Y)
B.Nc=new A.bD("Vedic chanting moves on three main notes. The ud\u0101tta is raised, the anud\u0101tta is lowered, and the svarita glides down from high to low. In printed texts they are shown with small marks above and below the letters.",null,null)
B.Nr=new A.bD("The note is not decoration. In the old teaching, a word chanted with the wrong note can change its meaning \u2014 the way a question and an answer can use the same words in a different tune.",null,null)
B.N8=new A.bD("Learn the notes with your hand. Many teachers move the hand up for the raised note, down for the low one, and sideways for the glide. The hand helps the voice remember.",null,null)
B.MY=new A.bD("We shall now explain how sounds are spoken. So begins the lesson on pronunciation.","\u015b\u012bk\u1e63\u0101\u1e43 vy\u0101khy\u0101sy\u0101ma\u1e25","Taittiriya Upanishad 1.2")
B.Nj=new A.bD("Be patient with yourself. Your voice will wander off the note many times. Each time, listen to the recording again and come back. This is how every student before you has learned.",null,null)
B.a7Q=s([B.Nc,B.Nr,B.N8,B.MY,B.Nj],t.L4)
B.Mz=new A.ib("The rise and the fall",68,B.a7Q)
B.Nn=new A.bD("In the ashram, new students are asked to listen to a chant three times before they say a word of it. It feels slow. It is the fastest way.",null,null)
B.Ng=new A.bD("Listening first lets the ear hold the whole shape of the chant \u2014 where it breathes, where it rises, where it rests. When you finally open your mouth, you are following a path you have already walked.",null,null)
B.N4=new A.bD("Use the slower speed in the app when you need it. Half speed is not a weakness; it is a magnifying glass. When the line feels easy, return to full speed.",null,null)
B.N5=new A.bD("Chant with others when you can. Your voice joins a larger sound and stops worrying about itself. Even alone, imagine the teacher sitting opposite you, chanting each line just before you.",null,null)
B.Np=new A.bD("At the end, stay quiet for a few breaths. The silence after a chant is part of the chant. Let it ring.",null,null)
B.a97=s([B.Nn,B.Ng,B.N4,B.N5,B.Np],t.L4)
B.Mr=new A.ib("Listening before chanting",124,B.a97)
B.MF=new A.bD("Most chants begin and end with Om. It is so familiar that we can say it without hearing it. Try, for one week, to chant it as if for the first time.",null,null)
B.ME=new A.bD("The old teachers heard three sounds in it \u2014 a, u and m \u2014 followed by a fourth that has no sound at all. The a opens in the throat, the u rolls forward over the tongue, the m closes the lips and hums. Then comes the silence, which belongs to the syllable as much as the sound does.",null,null)
B.N0=new A.bD("Om, the single syllable, is the vast reality.","om ity ek\u0101k\u1e63ara\u1e43 brahma","Bhagavad Gita 8.13")
B.Nv=new A.bD("Chant it three times before any practice. Let the first be for the body, the second for the mind, and the third for whatever is deeper than both. You need not believe anything to begin \u2014 only listen.",null,null)
B.MW=new A.bD("When the hum fades, do not hurry to the next thing. Sit inside the quiet it leaves behind. Many students find that this small pause becomes the most precious part of the day.",null,null)
B.a5g=s([B.MF,B.ME,B.N0,B.Nv,B.MW],t.L4)
B.Ms=new A.ib("The sound of Om",182,B.a5g)
B.a93=s([B.Mp,B.Mz,B.Mr,B.Ms],t.n4)
B.NG=new A.l_("sounds-veda","Sounds of the Veda",240,4.8,"Scripture","3 Mar 2026",B.Vl,"An introduction to why the Vedas are chanted the way they are: the three notes, the care given to every syllable, the old habit of listening before speaking, and the sound of Om. Written for beginners who want their chanting to feel steady and right.",B.a93,!1)
B.a88=s(["Letters to a","Seeker"],t.s)
B.TX=new A.i(1,0.14901960784313725,0.25098039215686274,0.1843137254901961,B.h)
B.U0=new A.i(1,0.3058823529411765,0.4627450980392157,0.3607843137254902,B.h)
