B.Vk=new A.zS("letter",B.a88,B.TX,B.U0,B.V4,B.S9,B.S7,B.S8,B.Sp,10)
B.MM=new A.bD("Dear seeker, you wrote that you do not know where to start, and that the books on your shelf seem to argue with each other. Let me answer simply: start where you are, with what you already have.",null,null)
B.N6=new A.bD("You have a breath. You have a few minutes in the morning. You have at least one prayer you learned as a child. That is enough to begin. The rest of the path shows itself only to those who are walking.",null,null)
B.Ny=new A.bD("Do not try to change everything in one week. Choose one practice and do it every day for forty days. If you miss a day, begin the count again \u2014 without drama, without guilt.",null,null)
B.Nh=new A.bD("Write to me again when the forty days are done. Tell me not what you felt, but what you noticed. With blessings, V. B.",null,null)
B.a9G=s([B.MM,B.N6,B.Ny,B.Nh],t.L4)
B.Mu=new A.ib("On beginning",7,B.a9G)
B.Nx=new A.bD("Dear seeker, you are worried because doubts come to you during your practice. Some days you wonder whether any of this is real. I am glad you told me. Doubt is not the enemy of faith; often it is the door to it.",null,null)
B.NC=new A.bD("A doubt that is hidden grows in the dark. A doubt that is asked honestly becomes a question \u2014 and a question can be studied, tested and lived.",null,null)
B.MS=new A.bD("So keep a small notebook. When a doubt comes, write it down and go on with your chanting. Read the notebook once a month. Some doubts will have dissolved on their own; others will have become your best teachers.",null,null)
B.Nt=new A.bD("The one who trusts gains knowledge.","\u015braddh\u0101v\u0101n labhate j\xf1\u0101nam","Bhagavad Gita 4.39")
B.MT=new A.bD("Trust here does not mean believing without thinking. It means staying long enough to find out. Stay. With blessings, V. B.",null,null)
B.a6f=s([B.Nx,B.NC,B.MS,B.Nt,B.MT],t.L4)
B.Mo=new A.ib("On doubt",38,B.a6f)
B.MV=new A.bD("Dear seeker, you asked whether you should leave your work in the city and come to live at the ashram, so that your practice can be pure. I understand the wish. But first, let us look at the word dharma together.",null,null)
B.MU=new A.bD("Dharma is not only religion, and it is not only rules. It is the order that holds a thing together \u2014 the coolness of water, the warmth of fire, the patience of a mother. Your own dharma is the part of that order that only you can carry.",null,null)
B.ML=new A.bD("Better is your own duty, even done imperfectly, than the duty of another done well.","\u015brey\u0101n svadharmo vigu\u1e47a\u1e25","Bhagavad Gita 3.35")
B.N1=new A.bD("Right now your dharma includes your parents, your colleagues and the work your hands know how to do. Doing these things honestly, and offering them quietly, is already sadhana. The ashram is not a place to escape your life; it is a place to learn how to return to it.",null,null)
B.No=new A.bD("So stay where you are for one more year. Chant in the morning, work well in the day, and visit us when the season allows. If the call is still there after a year, we will talk again. With blessings, V. B.",null,null)
B.a9h=s([B.MV,B.MU,B.ML,B.N1,B.No],t.L4)
B.Mw=new A.ib("On duty",66,B.a9h)
B.N9=new A.bD("Dear seeker, you say there is no one near you who shares this path, and that you feel alone when you sit for practice. Many have felt this. It is not a sign that you are on the wrong road.",null,null)
B.N2=new A.bD("Remember that every chant you say has been said by countless voices before you. When you chant the Shanti Mantra, you are joining a circle thousands of years wide.",null,null)
B.MQ=new A.bD("Still, find a little company if you can. One friend who chants with you on Sundays. The evening satsang. A visit to the ashram when the season allows. Company is not a crutch; it is a lamp held up beside your own.",null,null)
B.Nf=new A.bD("And on the days when you are truly alone, let that be a practice too. Solitude, held gently, becomes stillness. With blessings, V. B.",null,null)
B.a9k=s([B.N9,B.N2,B.MQ,B.Nf],t.L4)
B.Mx=new A.ib("On being alone",97,B.a9k)
B.a5z=s([B.Mu,B.Mo,B.Mw,B.Mx],t.n4)
B.NH=new A.l_("letters-seeker","Letters to a Seeker",128,2.6,"Teachings","20 Aug 2026",B.Vk,"Replies Guruji wrote to students who asked him for help \u2014 on beginning, on doubt, on duty and on walking the path alone. Each letter is short enough to read with your morning tea.",B.a5z,!1)
B.a5V=s(["Daily","Sadhana"],t.s)
B.UQ=new A.i(1,0.788235294117647,0.47058823529411764,0.10980392156862745,B.h)
B.Tq=new A.i(1,0.5568627450980392,0.23137254901960785,0.054901960784313725,B.h)
