B.Ve=new A.r8("vedic-chanting",!1,"Foundations of Vedic chanting","A gentle start for anyone who wants to chant well. Learn how to sit and breathe, why the tradition cares so much about correct sound, and how to chant your first two mantras slowly and clearly. Each lesson takes about ten minutes.",B.a67,"vedic")
B.a9P=s(["The G\u012bt\u0101 begins at the edge of a war.","Arjuna, a great warrior, suddenly cannot act.","Krishna, his friend and charioteer, begins to teach.","So the G\u012bt\u0101 starts where many of us are: confused."],t.s)
B.a3v=new A.h8("battlefield",B.hM,"A conversation on a battlefield",500,3,"Why does a book about inner peace begin on the edge of a war? A short talk on the setting of the G\u012bt\u0101.",B.a9P,B.bi,null,null,null,null,null,B.eV)
B.a47=s(["The Bhagavad G\u012bt\u0101 is part of the Mahabharata. Its seven hundred verses are mostly a dialogue between two people: Arjuna, a warrior prince, and Krishna, his friend and charioteer.","There is a frame around it. The blind king Dhritarashtra asks his minister Sanjaya what is happening on the battlefield, and Sanjaya, given special sight, describes it to him. So the whole G\u012bt\u0101 reaches us as a report.","Why does this matter? Because the G\u012bt\u0101 is a conversation. Arjuna asks real questions, doubts, argues and asks again. Krishna answers patiently, from many sides. You are invited to read it the same way \u2014 asking, not just accepting.","As you read, notice when Arjuna\u2019s questions sound like your own. That is usually where the G\u012bt\u0101 has something to teach you."],t.s)
B.a3t=new A.h8("who-speaks",B.eT,"Who is speaking, and to whom",0,3,"",B.bi,B.a47,null,null,null,null,null,B.eV)
B.a4o=s([B.a3v,B.a3t],t.Lo)
B.QW=new A.vb("Opening the G\u012bt\u0101",B.a4o)
B.a3A=new A.h8("verse-247",B.jr,"Listen: verse 2.47, slowly",250,3,"The well-known verse on action and its results, chanted slowly twice, followed by a short explanation.",B.bi,B.bi,"karma\u1e47y ev\u0101dhik\u0101ras te\nm\u0101 phale\u1e63u kad\u0101cana |\nm\u0101 karma-phala-hetur bh\u016br\nm\u0101 te sa\u1e45go \u2019stv akarma\u1e47i ||","2.47","Your right is to the work alone, never to its fruits. Do not let the fruit be your motive, and do not cling to doing nothing.",null,null,B.eV)
B.a8D=s(["Arjuna asks Krishna to be his teacher.","Krishna speaks of the Self that is never born and never dies.","He then turns to duty and right action."],t.s)
